adjacent|next-to|next to or sharing a boundary|adjective; adjacent to|B|Both sources describe buildings or rooms immediately next to another place. Keep the neighboring relation rather than split examples by buildings and rooms.
flour|ground-baking-powder|bột xay từ ngũ cốc hoặc thực vật dùng làm thức ăn|uncount food noun|A|The sources consistently describe powder used in food preparation. Flour can come from different plants; do not restrict it to wheat.
underestimate|judge-too-low|đánh giá thấp mức độ, năng lực hoặc giá trị của ai hay điều gì|transitive; underestimate ability or amount|A|The source says to think less of a person or thing than is warranted; losing because of the other team's skill supports judging ability too low. Keep the evidenced scope.
comparable|similar-enough-to-compare|tương tự để có thể so sánh|comparable to or with|B|Both sources describe similarity that permits comparison; results, costs and houses are contexts of one relation, not separate meanings.
exert|apply-force-or-influence|tác dụng hoặc tạo ra lực, ảnh hưởng hay áp lực|exert influence or force on something|A|Oxford examples separately name influence and physical force, both applied effects. Keep these source-backed collocations together unless evidence warrants a stronger lexical boundary.
exert|use-strength-or-effort|dùng sức lực hoặc khả năng để tạo ra tác động|exert strength or energy; exert oneself|B|The English Vocab source defines using strength or ability and gives energy while lifting weights. This differs from a force or influence exerted on an object.
side|lateral-part|phần bên hoặc khu vực dọc một vật hay nơi chốn|left or right side of a place|A|The stage example locates seats on a lateral part. Preserve the spatial meaning in one proposal.
side|surface-face|một mặt của vật có hai hay nhiều mặt|the other side of a flat object|A|The paper example names the reverse face, distinct from a lateral area of a venue.
side|party-in-conflict|một bên tham gia tranh chấp hoặc bất đồng|both sides in a dispute|A|Both sides agreed to stop fighting identifies opposing parties, a source-supported abstract use separate from physical sides.
deal|agreement|thỏa thuận giữa các bên|make or sign a deal|A|Both sources support a negotiated agreement between companies or people; the noun is countable in this use.
deal|handle-matter|xử lý hoặc giải quyết một vấn đề|deal with a problem or complaint|B|Oxford says managers deal with complaints, while the agreement noun is separately evidenced. Preserve deal with as the required construction.
chamber|enclosed-room|phòng kín hoặc phòng có mục đích riêng|in a chamber; chamber room|B|Sources describe a meeting room or council chamber. Keep the room sense distinct from a legislative body.
chamber|legislative-body|viện hoặc cơ quan lập pháp|one or more chambers of a legislature|A|Oxford explicitly says a legislature has two chambers, supporting the institutional body sense apart from a room.
seek|look-for-or-pursue|tìm kiếm hoặc cố đạt được điều gì|seek a solution; seek advice|B|The organization seeks a solution and a person sought advice. Both pursue something desired; the different object does not require separate meanings.
silence|absence-of-sound|sự vắng lặng, không có âm thanh|in silence; sudden silence|A|The sources explicitly define absence of sound or noise; room and students are contexts, not extra meanings.
shower|wash-under-spray|lần tắm dưới vòi sen|have or take a shower|B|Oxford quick and cool shower examples describe washing under water; retain this as the bathing-event noun.
shower|bathroom-fixture|thiết bị vòi sen trong phòng tắm|the shower; shower in a bathroom|A|Oxford says the shower in the bathroom is broken, clearly referring to the installed fixture, not the bathing event.
shower|brief-rainfall|cơn mưa rào ngắn|a shower of rain; short shower|A|Oxford's short shower that cooled the air supports a brief rainfall, distinct from bathing and the fixture.
miracle|seemingly-impossible-event|điều kỳ diệu dường như không thể xảy ra|a recovery or event seems like a miracle|A|Both sources describe an unexpected, seemingly impossible good event; recovery and a lost dog returning are contexts of the same meaning.
tyre|rubber-wheel-covering|lốp cao su bao quanh bánh xe|British spelling tyre; US tire|C|Oxford describes a bicycle tyre and provides US spelling tire. This is the same part with a regional spelling variant.
inmate|institution-resident|người bị giam hoặc cư trú trong một cơ sở khép kín|inmate of a prison or institution|A|The sources focus on prison and institutional residents. Keep the definition broad enough for the linked evidence without adding unsupported legal status.
manor|historic-large-house|nhà lớn thuộc một điền trang hoặc khu đất|a manor house; count noun|A|The source depicts a large many-roomed house with gardens. Avoid adding historical ownership or legal details absent from the evidence.
super|excellent-informal|rất tốt hoặc tuyệt vời theo cách thân mật|informal adjective before noun or predicative|B|Both sources use super for a very good time, meal or job. The contexts support one informal positive adjective sense.
payment|act-or-sum-paid|việc thanh toán hoặc khoản tiền được trả|make a payment; monthly payment|B|Sources support the act required before delivery and an amount due monthly; retain countability and both closely linked aspects in one source-limited entry.
errand|short-task-away|việc cần đi đâu đó để làm hoặc chuyển một việc|run or do an errand|A|The source defines a task involving going somewhere to buy, deliver or carry a message. Keep the everyday task scope without inventing other errands.
handy|useful-for-task|hữu ích hoặc thuận tiện cho một việc|handy for a purpose|A|Sources say a tool is handy for opening packages and easy to use; preserve practical usefulness as one sense.
handy|within-reach|ở gần và sẵn trong tầm tay khi cần|keep something handy|B|Oxford says to keep a notebook handy, meaning accessible when needed. This is distinct from usefulness for a task.
urgent|needs-immediate-action|cần được xử lý ngay vì không thể trì hoãn|urgent request or repairs|A|Both sources emphasize importance and immediate action for blood requests and roof repairs; these are contexts of one urgency sense.
